<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 27-day Cetes seen at 29.66 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 27-day Cetes seen at 29.66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 27-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 21 basis points to 29.66 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    27-DAY     29.45	    29.66		   + 21 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     28.90	    29.06		   + 16 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    27.69	    27.80		   + 11 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     27.15	    27.27		   + 12 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
</text>
